DevOps Interview Preparation
2–4 Years Experience | Tool 12 | GCP

DevOps & Advanced Cloud Concepts (Production Ready)

At 2–4 years, interviewers expect you to understand GCP services deeply, design scalable systems, and integrate CI/CD & automation.

🔹 Core GCP Interview Questions (2–4 yrs)

• Why choose GCP over other cloud providers?
• GCP global infrastructure (Regions, Zones)
• Project vs Folder vs Organization
• IAM in GCP — roles & service accounts
• What is a service account and why is it used?
• Compute Engine vs GKE vs Cloud Run
• Managed Instance Groups (MIG)
• Load Balancing in GCP (L7 vs L4)
• Cloud Storage classes
• Persistent Disk vs Filestore
• VPC — global vs regional concept

🔹 DevOps & CI/CD on GCP

• Cloud Build — how it works?
• Cloud Deploy — use cases
• Artifact Registry
• GCP with Jenkins / GitHub Actions
• GCP secrets management (Secret Manager)
• Infrastructure as Code in GCP (Terraform)
• GCP logging & monitoring (Cloud Logging, Cloud Monitoring)

🔹 Advanced GCP Concepts (Interview Favorite)

• GKE architecture (Control Plane vs Node Pools)
• Autopilot vs Standard GKE
• Node auto-provisioning
• Workload Identity — why it’s important?
• VPC Service Controls
• Private GKE clusters
• Multi-region deployments in GCP
• Blue-Green & Canary deployments on GKE
• Cost optimization in GCP

🔹 Real-World GCP Scenarios

• GKE pods not scaling — troubleshooting steps
• Permission denied error using service account — how to fix?
• Application not accessible through Load Balancer — checks?
• Sudden GCP cost spike — investigation approach
• CI/CD pipeline failing in Cloud Build — what will you check?

💡 Interview Tip:
If you say:
👉 “We use GKE with Workload Identity, private clusters, and Cloud Monitoring”
you already sound like a strong multi-cloud DevOps engineer.
